# Cloudflare WORKERS static-asset rewrites — keeps the original extensionless
# URLs (/contact, /projects, ...) working now that the files live in /pages/.
#
# This file must sit in the ASSETS DIRECTORY configured for the Worker (the
# wrangler.toml [assets] "directory", or whatever folder was uploaded as
# assets). Cloudflare parses it and does not serve it.
#
# Format:  <source>  <destination>  <code>
#   200 = proxy. The visitor's URL bar keeps showing /contact, so the existing
#         canonical tags and sitemap.xml stay valid.
#
# !! Do NOT replace this list with a blanket  /*  /pages/:splat  200  rule.
#    A splat also matches /css/style.css, /images/*, /js/main.js, /sitemap.xml
#    and the homepage, and these rules are applied to static asset responses --
#    so every asset would be proxied to a non-existent /pages/... path and the
#    site would render unstyled and imageless.
#
# Destination is deliberately extension-less: Workers' default html_handling
# ("auto-trailing-slash") serves /pages/contact from pages/contact.html, and
# requesting a *.html path directly triggers a 307 to the extension-less form.
#
# CAVEAT: _redirects is NOT applied to requests handled by Worker script code,
# and not applied at all when run_worker_first is enabled for the Worker.

